hwui's BitmapRegionDecoder, Gainmap, AnimatedImageDrawable, Mesh and MeshSpecification registered on the host flavor,
as Android registers them (ADR-0043 a2's open item: compiled but unregistered classes).

The host flavor compiles jni/BitmapRegionDecoder.cpp, jni/Gainmap.cpp, jni/AnimatedImageDrawable.cpp,
jni/MeshSpecification.cpp and jni/android_graphics_Mesh.cpp, but LayoutlibLoader's map does not name them, so an app
that decodes a region of an image (tiled image viewers), reads a photo's HDR gain map, shows an animated GIF or WebP
through ImageDecoder's drawable, or draws a custom mesh got an UnsatisfiedLinkError. All five draw on a CPU canvas.
So the map and the list of patch 0006 gain them, in the device's gRegJNI order. HardwareRendererObserver and
HardwareBufferRenderer stay out: they belong to hwui's GPU pipeline, which the host flavor does not run.

